# DECRQCRA, the checksum of a rectangle of the screen: CSI Pi ; Pg ; Pt ; Pl ; Pb ; Pr * y,
# answered DCS Pi ! ~ xxxx ST.
#
# The request lets a program read the screen back cell by cell, so a terminal answers it only when
# its host has switched that on (`screen-checksum allow`). The sum is xterm's with the checksum
# extension's bits 0 and 1: not negated and without the video attributes, so a cell is its code
# point, a blank (written or not) is a space and a rectangle is the sum of its cells modulo 65,536.

test DECRQCRA is not answered unless the host allows it
convention reading the screen back is a risk (a program, also over ssh, could read it cell by cell), so it starts off, as in xterm's default of leaving such reports off
size 10 3
feed a\e[1;0;1;1;1;1*y
reply none

test DECRQCRA of one cell is its code point
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA: the answer is DCS Pi ! ~ xxxx ST, four hex digits (xterm's checksum extension 3, unnegated, is the sum of the characters)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 10 3
feed a\e[7;0;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP7!~0061\e\\

test DECRQCRA of a rectangle is the sum of its cells
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA: the checksum of the rectangle, here the sum of the characters 0x61 + 0x62 + 0x63
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 10 3
feed abc\e[1;0;1;1;1;3*y
reply \eP1!~0126\e\\

test DECRQCRA counts a blank cell as a space
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA (checksum extension, bit 2: do not omit the checksum for blanks)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 10 3
feed \e[1;0;3;3;3;3*y
reply \eP1!~0020\e\\

test DECRQCRA counts an erased cell as a space
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA (checksum extension, bit 2: do not omit the checksum for blanks)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 10 3
feed x\e[1;1H\e[K\e[2;0;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP2!~0020\e\\

test DECRQCRA without an area sums the page
spec VT510 DECRQCRA: the area is as in DECCARA, whose Pt and Pl default to 1 and Pb and Pr to the last line and column
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 2 2
feed ab\r\ncd\e[4;0*y
reply \eP4!~018A\e\\

test DECRQCRA without parameters sums the page and answers for request 0
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA: Pi is echoed; VT510: missing parameters are 0 or their defaults
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 2 2
feed ab\r\ncd\e[*y
reply \eP0!~018A\e\\

test DECRQCRA echoes its request number
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA: Pi is the request id, answered as DCS Pi ! ~ xxxx ST
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed \e[65535;1;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP65535!~0020\e\\

test DECRQCRA is cut to the screen
spec VT510 DECCARA, the area's parameters: values beyond the page's width or height are treated as that dimension
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 2 2
feed ab\r\ncd\e[1;0;2;2;99;99*y
reply \eP1!~0064\e\\

test DECRQCRA of an upside-down area sums nothing
spec VT510 DECCARA, the area's parameters: Pt must not exceed Pb (the area has no cells)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed abcd\e[1;0;2;1;1;1*y
reply \eP1!~0000\e\\

test DECRQCRA counts from the region in origin mode
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA: the area is affected by origin mode (DECOM), as DECCARA's
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 3
feed abcd\r\nefgh\r\nijkl\e[2;3r\e[?6h\e[1;0;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP1!~0065\e\\

test DECRQCRA counts a wide character once
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA (checksum extension, bit 4 off: the cell's character; the second half of a wide character has none)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed \u{65e5}\e[1;0;1;1;1;2*y
reply \eP1!~65E5\e\\

test DECRQCRA ignores combining marks
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA (checksum extension, bit 4 off: combining characters are ignored)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed e\u{301}\e[1;0;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP1!~0065\e\\

test DECRQCRA ignores the video attributes
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA (checksum extension, bit 1: do not report the VT100 video attributes)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed \e[1;7;4;5ma\e[1;0;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP1!~0061\e\\

test DECRQCRA sums modulo 65536
spec xterm ctlseqs DECRQCRA: a 16-bit checksum, four hex digits (2,000 cells of 0x7A add up to 244,000 = 0xB920 + 3 * 65,536)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 80 25
repeat 2000 z
feed \e[1;0*y
reply \eP1!~B920\e\\

test DECRQCRA of a page other than the first is not answered
spec VT510 DECRQCRA: Pg is the page; the terminal has one page
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed a\e[1;2;1;1;1;1*y
reply none

test DECRQCRA of the first page is answered
spec VT510 DECRQCRA: Pg is the page (0 is the current one, 1 the first)
known-fail: alacritty – DECRQCRA is not answered
screen-checksum allow
size 4 2
feed a\e[1;1;1;1;1;1*y
reply \eP1!~0061\e\\
